{title: 178 - The Unveiled Christ}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #178 • UNVEILED • 14.16.15.16}
{lyricist: N. B. Herrell}
{composer: N. B. Herrell}
{key: Db}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 178}
{meta: tune UNVEILED}
{meta: meter 14.16.15.16}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Db/Ab]Once our blessed Christ of beauty [Ab7/Gb]Was veiled [Ab]off from human view;
[Db/Ab]But through suffering, death and sorrow He has rent the veil in two.
[Ab]O behold [Fm]the Man [Ebm/Gb]of Sorrows, O behold [Ab7/Gb]Him in plain [Db/F]view;
[Gb]Lo! He is the mighty Conqueror, [Ab7]Since [Gb]He rent [Gdim]the veil [Fm]in two.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Ab]O [Ab7/C]behold [Db]the Man of [Db7/B]Sorrows!
[Bbm]O behold Him in plain view!
[Db]Lo! He is [Ab7]the mighty Conqueror
[Gb/Db]Since He rent the veil in two;
[Gb/Db]Lo! He [Db]is [Ab]the mighty [Ebm/Bb]Conqueror
[Db/F]Since He rent the veil in two.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Db/Ab]Yes, He is with [Ab7/Gb]God, [Ab]the Father,
[Db/Ab]Interceding there for you;
[Ab]For [Ab7/Gb]He [Fm]is [Ebm/Gb]the Well [Ab7/Gb]beloved
[Gb]Since He rent [Fm]the [Ab7]veil [Gb]in [Gdim]two.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Db/Ab]Holy angels [Ab7/Gb]bow [Ab]before Him,
[Db/Ab]Men of earth give praises due;
[Ab]For [Ab7/Gb]He [Fm]is [Ebm/Gb]the mighty Conqueror
[Gb]Since He rent [Fm]the [Ab7]veil [Gb]in [Gdim]two.
{end_of_verse}
